# cvvdp vs buttloop tracking benchmark

**Started**: 2026-05-24
**RFC**: `docs/RFC_CVVDP_FORK.md`

## Methodology

For every (image, distance, effort, backend) cell:

1. Encode with the named backend (butteraugli or cvvdp; CPU or GPU).
2. Decode via jxl-oxide (linear sRGB output).
3. Compute every available perceptual metric on the decoded image vs
   source. Persist all of them — single source-of-truth for any future
   reweighting.

## Backends

| tag         | crate path                                   | feature flag                                      |
|---          |---                                           |---                                                |
| `B`         | `butteraugli::ButteraugliReference` (CPU)    | `butteraugli-loop` (default)                      |
| `B_GPU`     | `butteraugli-gpu::Butteraugli` (CUDA)        | `butteraugli-loop gpu-butteraugli`                |
| `C_GPU`     | `cvvdp-gpu::Cvvdp` (CUDA)                    | `cvvdp-loop`                                      |
| `C_CPU`     | `cvvdp-cpu::Cvvdp` (port, Phase 5)           | `cvvdp-loop cvvdp-loop-cpu`                       |
| `C_GPU_v4`  | `cvvdp-gpu::Cvvdp` + Phase 8d tighten + Phase 8g constants | `cvvdp-loop cvvdp-loop-tighten`     |

## Phase 8f (2026-05-25): C_GPU_v4 added

C_GPU_v4 rows added 2026-05-25 by the Phase 8f validation sweep on the
post-Phase-8g encoder (`commit=689ba0df`). The C_GPU_v4 dispatch:

- `LossyConfig::with_cvvdp_loop(Some(true))` — enables the cvvdp buttloop
  (same as `C_GPU`)
- `LossyConfig::with_cvvdp_bytes_tighten(Some(true))` — enables the
  Phase 8d tighten exit pass
- Phase 8g k_tile_norm=0.16 per-block reducer constant applies
  automatically when the `cvvdp-loop` feature is compiled in

Required features: `gpu-butteraugli butteraugli-loop cvvdp-loop cvvdp-loop-cpu cvvdp-loop-tighten ssim2-loop parallel`.

C_GPU_v4 is the cvvdp-fork's shipped production default when the cargo
features are compiled in. See `docs/CVVDP_FORK_DECISION.md` for the
Phase 8f decision-rule application.

## Corpus

- **CID22-512** (41 photos, held out from W44 training, validation/ dir)
- **GB82-SC** (11 screenshots — codec_wiki/gmessages/graph/gui/imac_dark/imac_g3/imac_g3_strip/imessage/terminal/windows/windows95)
- **W44-PHASE4-S1 extras** (2 distinct images: baby-lossless / bulb-lossless under codec-corpus/gb82/)

Note on W44-S1: the actual `pick_w44_phase4_s1_corpus()` selects 27 images,
but 25 already overlap with CID22 validation + GB82-SC. Only baby-lossless
and bulb-lossless are NEW vs the other two corpora. So 54 distinct images
total.

The RFC §5.1 figure of "101 images × 21 cells = 2,121" was aspirational
(based on an early 50-image W44-S1 sample). The actual unique-image
count from the available local corpora is 54 → 54 × 21 = **1,134 cells
per backend**. The D1 baseline pass targets full coverage of these.

## Backends populated by D1 (this commit)

- `B` rows = production-default encoder (`EncoderStrategy::Zenjxl`,
  `LossyConfig::new(d).with_effort(e)`, butteraugli CPU buttloop default)
- `score_butter_cpu`: `butteraugli::butteraugli_linear` (linear-f32)
- `score_butter_gpu`: `butteraugli_gpu::Butteraugli<CudaRuntime>::new_multires`
  on sRGB-u8 — parity-check column. Both reference + distorted re-encoded
  to sRGB-u8 from the decoded linear-f32, so this measures GPU butteraugli
  on the SAME pixels as the CPU column.
- `score_cvvdp_gpu`: `cvvdp_gpu::CvvdpOpaque::new(Cuda, w, h, default).compute_srgb_u8`
- `score_cvvdp_cpu`: NA (Agent A's CPU port not landed yet)
- `score_ssim2`: `fast_ssim2::compute_ssimulacra2` on sRGB-u8

## Encode timing

`wall_ms` is the median of 3 sequential encodes per cell, single-process,
multi-threaded encoder (no `with_threads(1)` override — we let the
default rayon pool fan out, matching production behaviour). The harness
short-circuits to 1 sample when the first iter exceeds 30s.

## Decode

jxl-oxide 0.12.5 fork (imazen/jxl-oxide fd4e2c3 per workspace
`[patch.crates-io]`) decoding to linear sRGB f32 via
`request_color_encoding(srgb_linear, RenderingIntent::Relative)`. This
matches the `quality_compare` harness and the CLAUDE.md "jxl-oxide
linear output" rule.

## Linear→sRGB-u8 round-trip

For SSIM2 and the GPU metrics (which take sRGB u8), we re-encode the
decoded linear-f32 via the explicit sRGB transfer function (linear
segment below 0.003_130_8, then `1.055 * x^(1/2.4) - 0.055`). This
matches the `quality_compare` `linear_to_srgb_u8`. We do NOT use the
input PNG bytes for the metric source — that would invoke
PNG-color-metadata divergence (see CLAUDE.md "CRITICAL: PNG Color
Metadata"). We use the PNG's decoded sRGB u8 (i.e., the encoder input)
as the reference; the GPU metric `ref_srgb` is the PNG's sRGB u8
directly, since the encoder ingests sRGB-u8 → linear internally before
encoding. This means butter_gpu's reference is `src_pixels_u8` and its
distorted is `decoded_linear → linear_to_srgb_u8`. butter_cpu's
reference is `src_pixels_u8 → srgb_to_linear` and distorted is the
decoded linear directly.

The two paths are NOT identical (CPU stays in linear domain
end-to-end; GPU round-trips through sRGB). Expect butter_cpu ≈
butter_gpu within ~5% on most cells; large divergences are documented
in `notes`.

## Schema

- `image`: image basename (no path)
- `corpus`: one of `CID22`, `GB82-SC`, `W44-S1`
- `effort`: encoder effort 5/7/8
- `distance`: encoder distance parameter
- `backend`: one of `B`, `B_GPU`, `C_GPU`, `C_CPU`, `C_GPU_v4`
- `bytes`: encoded file size in bytes
- `wall_ms`: encode wall time (best-of-3 median, single-thread unless noted)
- `score_butter_cpu`: Rust butteraugli max-norm on decoded vs source (smaller = better)
- `score_butter_gpu`: butteraugli-gpu max-norm (parity check)
- `score_cvvdp_gpu`: cvvdp-gpu JOD (10 = perfect, lower = worse)
- `score_cvvdp_cpu`: cvvdp-cpu JOD (Phase 5+)
- `score_ssim2`: SSIMULACRA2 (legacy reference)
- `notes`: free-form (e.g. backend fallbacks, divergence-detector trips)

## Decision direction

Per RFC §5.4:
- Ship cvvdp default-ON only if it strictly Pareto-dominates butteraugli
  on ≥1 corpus AND comes within 5% on the others (bytes axis).
- Otherwise: ship opt-in only.

## Phase tags (rows added per phase landing)

- `phase1`: cvvdp-gpu diffmap API smoke (no encoder change, baseline)
- `phase2`: PerceptualBackend rename (byte-identical, sanity row)
- `phase3`: CvvdpBackend wired but not default
- `phase4`: full cvvdp-loop opt-in encodes
- `phase5`: cvvdp-cpu integrated
- `phase6`: final tracking sweep + decision

## Reproducibility

Each row carries the commit SHA of the encoder at time of measurement.
Append-only; never edit historical rows. Methodology changes get a new
TSV file + meta with the date.

## Pre-analysis row filter

The Phase 6 sweep introduced multi-line panic backtraces from transient
CUDA hiccups that break TSV row alignment (~9 rows per backend sweep).
Phase 8f preserves the precedent: pre-filter via `awk -F'\t' 'NR==1 || NF==13'`
before feeding to `scripts/cvvdp_pareto_*.py`. Phase 6 had 27 such rows
filtered; Phase 8f added 60 more (totals: 87 malformed rows of 5757
data rows). The clean derived file is NOT committed; the awk filter is
documented here and runs deterministically off the raw TSV.

## Phase 8f run record (2026-05-25)

- Host: `lilith` (Linux 6.6.114.1-microsoft-standard-WSL2 / RTX 5070 / CUDA 13.2)
- Encoder commit: `689ba0df` (Phase 8g — per-block reducer constants refit)
- Backend swept: `C_GPU_v4` only (rows appended; B/B_GPU/C_GPU/C_CPU unchanged)
- Run wall: 916s (~15.3 min) for 1,134 cells (1.24 cells/s avg)
- Rows populated: **1,134 of 1,134** (100% emitted; 29 OOM cells have
  bytes=0/score=NA but row exists; coverage of valid scoring cells:
  1,105 / 1,134 = 97.4%)
- 29 cells failed encode with `LimitExceeded` ("memory budget exceeded:
  ~135-160 MB on top of ~2.0 GiB, cap 2 GiB"). All GB82-SC e=8 d≥1.5 on
  6 of the 11 screenshots: codec_wiki, gmessages, imac_dark, imac_g3,
  imac_g3_strip (each on 5 distances d∈{1.5,2,3,4,5}), imessage (d=4,5),
  windows (d=4,5). The OOM cluster is larger than Phase 6's 3-cell OOM
  set because the Phase 8d tighten exit pass adds extra per-iter encodes
  that increase memory pressure on the same screenshots. Per Phase 6
  precedent these cells are documented and the OOM is a memory budget
  configuration issue, not a structural bitstream bug.
- Per-corpus row counts (header excluded, C_GPU_v4 rows only):
  - CID22: 861 (41 imgs × 21 cells)
  - GB82-SC: 231 (11 imgs × 21 cells, 29 OOM)
  - W44-S1: 42 (2 imgs × 21 cells)
- Build features: `__expert butteraugli-loop cvvdp-loop cvvdp-loop-cpu
  cvvdp-loop-tighten gpu-butteraugli ssim2-loop parallel`

